      <strong>Working Group</strong>
      <span>2006 &#8211; 2018</span>
    </div>
    <div class="mgdb-hero-body">
      <h1 id="working-group-title">The MaizeGDB Working Group.</h1>
      <p class="mgdb-hero-description">An outside group of maize researchers and database developers, chosen for breadth of expertise, that reviewed the MaizeGDB project and issued written guidance to it. The group continued the work begun by the ten-person <a href="#wg-steering">Steering Committee</a> that guided the MaizeDB to MaizeGDB transition, whose roster is recorded here too. This is the record of both: nine members on the last Working Group roster, sixteen who served before them, the ten who steered the transition, and nineteen documents exchanged with the MaizeGDB team between 2006 and 2018.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="mgdb-message mgdb-message-info wg-archive-note" role="status">
    <div><strong>Archive notice.</strong> MaizeGDB does not currently have an active Working Group. The most recent documented exchange is from September 2018. This page is the historical record and is no longer updated.</div>
  </div>

